{
  "q1_accurate": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "Server (nomad/server.go)", "note": "Delivered the entire audit: affected_via_composition gave every direct *Server field holder with file:line (all A1/A2/A3 rows), and retained_via_interfaces gave all narrowed-interface holders (B1-B17) with via/carrier/chain — the backbone of Steps 4-7, cited verbatim"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "NewServer (callees)", "note": "Located every subsystem wiring call in the constructor (newPlanner plan_apply.go:39, NewPeriodicDispatch periodic.go:140, NewEncrypter encrypter.go:91, setupNodeDrainer/setupVolumeWatcher/setupWorkers) used in Step 2"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "RPCer (client/config/arconfig.go, callers)", "note": "inherited_by gave the exact runtime satisfier set {client.Client, agent.Agent, nomad.Server, TestAgent}, which anchored the Step 5/6 runtime caveat that the blast could not resolve alone"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "cluster server object that runs the scheduler and handles RPCs", "note": "Top-ranked nomad.Server methods in nomad/server.go, correctly identifying the target type immediately"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "Planner (scheduler/structs/structs.go)", "note": "symbol_not_found because I pinned the wrong file, but the error's 'elsewhere' field gave the correct location scheduler/structs/interfaces.go:108 so no wasted turn"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "RPCer (no file)", "note": "Returned ambiguous (4 matches) rather than an answer — expected for an overloaded name; top_matches let me re-query with the right file"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "Method bodies — blast/graph gave every holder's file:line but not the code behavior; I Read drainer_shims.go, periodic.go, plan_apply.go, arconfig.go, config.go to describe HOW each narrowed handle reaches the server (e.g. drainerShim.NodesDrainComplete calling s.raftApply), which is content Sense correctly does not carry"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "NewServer callees", "fallback": "read", "missing": "Struct field comments/ownership for Step 2 'state that outlives a request' — I Read server.go:150-329 and Shutdown :744 for the field list and teardown sequence, not locatable via edges"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "Planner in scheduler/structs/structs.go", "query_after": "read scheduler/structs/interfaces.go:108 directly", "hint": "\"symbol exists outside the pinned file — elsewhere: structs.Planner scheduler/structs/interfaces.go:108\""},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "RPCer (unqualified)", "query_after": "RPCer with file=client/config/arconfig.go", "hint": "\"Multiple symbols named RPCer exist — retry with the file parameter ... see top_matches\""}
  ],
  "q4_value": "One sense_blast on nomad.Server returned the complete two-part holder set — direct *Server fields AND holders behind locally-declared interfaces (retained_via_interfaces with carrier+chain) — including client-side RPCer holders that never import or name the server package, which grep for '*Server' would have entirely missed and which were the explicit easy-to-miss target of the ticket.",
  "q5_improve": "retained_via_interfaces marks the runtime satisfier as unverified but picks one carrier (agent.Agent > Server) per row; surfacing the full satisfier set inline (as the separate RPCer graph call had to) would have flagged the client.Client-vs-Server ambiguity for B11-B17 without a second query.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "Per Q1, a single sense_blast produced the transitive interface-retention audit — client holders behind local RPCer interfaces that name no server type — which grep/read could not have assembled this session, and the only fallbacks (Q2) were for method bodies Sense is not meant to carry."
}

